{"id":"anti-example-001","type":"pattern","fact":"Example: NEVER use 'as any' type casting - it hides bugs and defeats TypeScript's type system.","recommendation":"Use proper type narrowing, generics, or 'as unknown as Type' for test mocks.","confidence":"high","provenance":[{"source":"documentation","reference":"TypeScript patterns guide","date":"2026-01-09"}],"tags":["typescript","type-safety"],"affectedFiles":["**/*.ts"],"affectedServices":[],"createdAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","updatedAt":"2026-01-09T00:00:00Z","usageCount":0,"helpfulCount":0,"outdatedReports":0}
{"id": "anti-ui-progress-by-file-count-001", "type": "pattern", "fact": "Counting touched files overstates UI progress. 23 of 27 screens had been 'restyled' with 6-12 line class swaps and were reported as implemented; the artboard layouts had not been built at all. The real work showed up as 100-250 line rewrites per screen (RegisterScreen 245, LoginScreen 138, MyOrdersScreen 131) — an order of magnitude more than the swap-only diffs.", "recommendation": "Report visual work by per-file diff magnitude against the base branch (git diff --stat main -- <screens>), not by the number of files touched, and state plainly which screens only received token swaps. A 10-line diff on a screen is a palette change, not a layout implementation.", "confidence": "high", "provenance": [{"source": "agent", "reference": "specs/017-ui-refresh self-reflect", "date": "2026-11-06"}], "tags": ["reporting", "ui", "verification", "agent-workflow"], "affectedFiles": ["mobile/src/screens/**/*.tsx"], "affectedServices": [], "createdAt": "2026-11-06T00:00:00Z", "updatedAt": "2026-11-06T00:00:00Z", "usageCount": 0, "helpfulCount": 0, "outdatedReports": 0}
